data.reasoningText:
The user wants: when the input is cleared and Enter is pressed, the search filter should be cleared (reset), which would trigger a refetch with no search filter.

Currently the Enter handler is:
```tsx
if (event.key === "Enter" && !searchOptionsOpen) {
  event.preventDefault();
  if (searchText.trim()) void refetchEncounters();
}
```

When `searchText` is empty and Enter is pressed, nothing happens. The user wants it to clear the `with`/`value` params (effectively resetting the search filter), which would update the query key and trigger a refetch.

The fix: when Enter is pressed with empty `searchText`, call `updateQuery({ with: undefined, value: undefined })` to clear the search params.

